{{Quote|It's a sad little slum named for the Imperial governor who kicked everybody out of their homes in Tangletown, and other outlying communities. Typical. Those in power don't ask, they just take.|Ezra Bridger, on Tarkintown|<ref name="Rebel Journal" />}}
'''Tangletown''' was a small, once-thriving [[farm]]ing [[City|community]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Lothal]]. It proudly referred to itself as the "[[Foodstuff|Food]] Basket of Lothal" due to its production of [[fruit]]s, [[spice]]s, [[vegetable]]s, and other flavors. In addition to agricultural importance, Tangletown also promoted itself as the "Relaxation Oasis of the Outer Rim," featuring a historic downtown that served as a tourist attraction.

During the [[Imperial Era]], the [[Galactic Empire]] occupied Lothal and began [[mining]] its land for [[ore]]. [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] ordered the forced displacement of Tangletown's citizens, leading to the relocation of its residents and those of other outlying farming communities to a re-settlement camp that came to be derisively known as [[Lothal re-settlement camp 43|Tarkintown]].

==Description==
{{Quote|Visit our Historic Downtown. Relaxation Oasis of the Outer Rim.|Tangletown tourism poster|<ref name="Rebel Journal" />}}
Tangletown was a small,<ref name="Comprehensive Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> developed [[Farm|agricultural]] [[City|settlement]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Lothal]] with a strong connection to the planet's farming industry. The town was known for its production of [[fruit]]s, [[spice]]s,<ref name="Rebel Journal" /> [[vegetable]]s,<ref name="Absolutely Everything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> and other flavors, earning it the moniker of the "[[Foodstuff|Food]] Basket of Lothal." It boasted a historic downtown that locals encouraged tourists to visit, touting itself as the "Relaxation Oasis of the Outer Rim."<ref name="Rebel Journal" /> Beneath Tangletown were rich veins of [[ore]] that could be used for industrial purposes.<ref name="Rebel Bluff">{{InsiderCite|158|Rebel Bluff|reprint=1}}</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|My research for the Mining Institute concluded that a rich vein of ore lay below these people's farms. I personally convinced the Grand Moff that mining would be worth the effort. At the time, I believed the Empire was a force for good, and would help lift Lothal out of poverty and obscurity.|Ria Clarr, who felt personally responsible for the plight of Tarkintown|<ref name="Rebel Bluff" />}}
[[File:Tarkin_town.png|thumb|250px|right|Tangletown's residents were forcibly relocated to Lothal re-settlement camp 43, derisively nicknamed Tarkintown.]]
Before the [[Galactic Empire]] occupied Lothal, Tangletown flourished as an agricultural center. [[Chef]] [[Strono Tuggs]] once visited Tangletown and sampled the [[Jogan Fruit Greens]] [[salad]] prepared by the locals.<ref name="Ultimate Cookbook">''[[Star Wars: The Ultimate Cookbook]]''</ref> The Empire's arrival changed everything, and the town became a target for Imperial expansion after the [[analyst]] [[Ria Clarr]] of the [[Imperial Mining Institute]] recommended to<ref name="Rebel Bluff" />  [[Grand Moff]]<ref name="Spark of Rebellion">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Spark of Rebellion]]''</ref> [[Wilhuff Tarkin]]<ref name="Rebel Bluff" />&mdash;[[Governor]] of the Outer Rim Territories<ref name="Spark of Rebellion" />&mdash;that farming communities<ref name="Rebel Journal" /> with rich, underground ore deposits<ref name="Rebel Bluff" /> like Tangletown<ref name="Rebel Journal" /> be mined for their resources.<ref name="Rebel Bluff" /> 

Under Tarkin's orders, the Empire forcibly relocated the citizens of Tangletown and nearby farming communities from their homes<ref name="Rebel Journal" /> and into what the Empire designated [[Lothal re-settlement camp 43]].<ref name="Rebel Bluff" /> The settlement became derisively known as Tarkintown, where the former citizens of Tangletown lived in impoverished conditions<ref name="Spark of Rebellion" /> as part of a growing [[refugee]] crisis on Lothal.<ref name="Nexus of Power">''[[Nexus of Power]]''</ref> [[Ezra Bridger]], a Lothalite orphan who became one of the [[Spectres|rebels]] who began operating on Lothal in [[5 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> mentioned the forced relocation of Tangletown's citizens to Tarkintown in his [[Rebel Journal|journal]], along with a town tourism poster promoting Tangletown's historic downtown,<ref name="Rebel Journal" /> published no earlier than the same [[Standard year|year]].<ref name="Date">''[[Rebel Journal by Ezra Bridger]]'' establishes that [[Rebel Journal|Ezra Bridger's journal]] was completed following the events of ''[[Star Wars Rebels: Spark of Rebellion]]''. As ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates ''Spark of Rebellion'' to [[5 BBY]], the work must have been finished by no earlier than that [[Standard year|year]].</ref>

In [[4 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines" /> during the [[Siege of Lothal]], the Empire burned Tarkintown to the ground as [[Reprisal Activities (Lothal)|reprisal]] for rebel aid and activity in the area, leaving the citizens who survived the razing once again displaced as [[prison]]ers of the Empire.<ref name="The Siege of Lothal">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Siege of Lothal]]''</ref> Tuggs referenced his visit to Tangletown in his third cookbook, ''[[The Ultimate Cookbook]]'',<ref name="Ultimate Cookbook">''[[Star Wars: The Ultimate Cookbook]]''</ref> which was published in [[35 ABY]].<ref name="TUC date">{{UltimateCookbookDate}}</ref>

==Inhabitants==
{{Quote|Greetings from Beautiful Tangletown.|Tangletown tourism poster|<ref name="Rebel Bluff" />}}
Tangletown was a farming community with a diverse, multi-species citizenry<ref name="Comprehensive Encyclopedia" /> that took pride in their town's agricultural success and cultural identity, encouraging visitors to make their way to the town. The citizens, who were mostly farmers,<ref name="Build the Millennium Falcon 25">{{BuildFalconCite|25|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> cultivated a variety of crops, including fruits, vegetables, and spices, which contributed to Tangletown's reputation as the "Food Basket of Lothal."<ref name="Rebel Journal" /> The forced removal of Tangletown's citizens by Imperial forces devastated their way of life, forcing them into impoverished conditions in Tarkintown and severing them from the once-thriving community they had built.<ref name="Spark of Rebellion" />

==Behind the scenes==
Tangletown was first indirectly mentioned in the first part of ''[[Star Wars Rebels: Spark of Rebellion]]'',<ref name="Spark of Rebellion" /> the two-part premiere episode of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'', which premiered on [[September 26]], [[2014]].<ref name="Insider 156">{{InsiderCite|156|Star Wars Rebels Recounted|''Star Wars Rebels'' Recounted}}</ref> It was later identified in the book ''[[Rebel Journal by Ezra Bridger]]'', written by [[Daniel Wallace]]<ref name="Rebel Journal" /> and released on [[October 21]] of the same year.<ref name="Studio">{{StudioFun|url=books/star-wars-rebels-rebel-journal-by-ezra-bridger-9780794432683|text=Star Wars Rebels: Rebel Journal by Ezra Bridger}}</ref>

